        skos:definition        "Lanes of mutually agreed upon tow lane areas, as agreed by Tow boat operators and local fixed gear fishermen. Prior to the establishment of such lanes it was not uncommon for tugs to collide with crabbing gear, causing damage to hulls and propulsion systems and losses of costly crab pots."@en;
        skos:inScheme          <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/ICANCOERO/current/> , <http://vocab.nerc.ac.uk/scheme/OCACETHES/current/>;
